&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Engineer – Multi-Region &amp;amp; Internationalisation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Engineer – Internationalisation Programme (Go, Kubernetes, Kafka, Cassandra, Postgres)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A global sports business is taking its platform international, and we need the architecture lead for the programme. You will be the subject-matter expert the whole programme leans on. That means guiding the shared services work, keeping the flagship consumer app on track, and covering the platform wherever services meet. It is a broad remit, and it is hands-on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The programme&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The client&#39;s shared services team supports several business lines. They are internationalising their flagship app alongside the shared services behind it, such as identity, loyalty and partner integrations. The first target is an isolated region with its own data-residency stack. Multi-region rollouts follow through 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setting the architecture direction across the shared services, and making sure each one can run inside an isolated region with no hidden dependency on the original one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeping the flagship app&#39;s internationalisation coherent as the services underneath it change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the seams: how the shared services interact across and within regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data residency: deciding what data is shared, what stays regional and what never leaves a region, across Cassandra and Postgres.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kafka in both worlds: self-contained within an isolated region, and replicated across regions where it is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Terraform and Kubernetes that stand up a new region repeatably, with explicit regional config and visible drift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross functional stakeholder management. You will be the glue between multiple teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first two weeks&lt;/strong&gt; you will review what the client&#39;s team has already built for the first region. You will come back with an honest verdict on what holds up, what will block an isolated launch, and what will make multi-region harder later.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will likely have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stood production systems up in new, isolated regions under data-residency rules, and taken systems multi-region, including the data and failover decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Been the architecture lead across several teams or services, not just one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current, senior Go, and enough React to change it with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of Cassandra, Postgres and Kafka in distributed setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes and Terraform experience at the level of designin

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About AlphaSense:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AlphaSense is the AI platform redefining market intelligence and workflow orchestration, trusted by thousands of leading organizations to drive faster, more confident decisions in business and finance. The platform combines domain-specific AI with a vast content universe of over 500 million premium business documents — including equity research, earnings calls, expert interviews, filings, news, and internal proprietary content. Purpose-built for speed, accuracy, and enterprise-grade security, AlphaSense helps teams extract critical insights, uncover market-moving trends, and automate complex workflows with high-quality outputs. With AI solutions like Generative Search, Generative Grid, and Deep Research, AlphaSense delivers the clarity and depth professionals need to navigate complexity and obtain accurate, real-time information quickly. For more information, visit &lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.alpha-sense.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.alpha-sense.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;. Come join us.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Core Cloud Platform team is responsible for AlphaSense&#39;s entire cloud infrastructure, including AWS account management, networking, data storages, and Kubernetes clusters. We build the underlying platform that supports hundreds of services and is used by over 400 globally distributed engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re scaling into a cell-based architecture, and the number of cells we run is growing fast, taking our Kubernetes footprint from dozens of clusters toward hundreds. That takes the platform in three directions at once: infrastructure configuration becomes a first-class layer with its own lifecycle, independent of application code; provisioning a new cell becomes a days-long automated operation rather than a multi-week effort; and cross-cell control points become standard, reusable, and consistent everywhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a Principal Engineer role with real breadth within the cloud platform. You&#39;ll set the architectural roadmap for our cloud, Kubernetes, and storage platform as it scales with AlphaSense&#39;s growth, and take dedicated ownership of the cloud-side configuration and Helm chart layer that every service depends on. Data storages are a critical part of this surface, and we&#39;re looking for genuine depth there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It requires a deep cloud of both operational and software development skills, the ability to lead ambitious technical programmes, and the credibility to set direction with Engineering leaders and very senior engineers across dozens of teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who genuinely embraces AI tooling in their day-

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer - Distributed Systems (ODP Governance)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ODP Governance is a cross platform team working in the biggest Datadog products (Metrics, Logs, APM) with the mission of giving customers governance tools to control costs and data hygiene of their telemetry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team builds cost controls and governance tools that help Datadog’s enterprise customers manage data ingestion, reduce unwanted data, and prioritize the telemetry that delivers the most value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our scope spans multiple Datadog products, including Metrics, Events, Logs, and APM. As a backend engineering team, we partner with these product teams to address recurring customer challenges that create operational friction, increase costs, and contribute to churn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also identify opportunities to extend successful capabilities across products—for example, adapting a control developed for Logs to support APM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships that it builds, the creativity it brings to the table, and the collaboration of being together. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our employees can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build performant high scale distributed systems to handle the load of Datadog’s biggest products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships across teams and independently seek out the information needed to move work forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become productive in unfamiliar systems and navigate ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate technical dependencies and integration challenges early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognize when a solution could benefit another product and take the initiative to explore it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect engineering decisions to customer value, cost efficiency, and usability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
